('Ankur Mittal', 'Inflection Point Ventures (IPV)', 'Identified', 'P4', 'Angel Platform', 'ipventures.in', 'ipventures.in', 'Use AFTER lead investor confirmed. Good for filling round quickly.', '2026-04-15', 'Most active by volume (45 investments in 2025). Fast process. Sector agnostic. Speed is the value.', '1–3 Cr (assembled)', 'Fast capital for round fill. Not thesis-driven.', '✅ None', 'Seed'),
('Hari Gopalakrishnan', 'Creaegis', 'Identified', 'P4', 'VC — Later Stage', 'creaegis.com', 'Warm intro only', 'Series C target. Keep on radar.', '2026-05-01', 'Led Third Wave Coffee Series C ($35M). PE firm comfortable with offline consumer. Entry point = Series C.', '100–300 Cr', 'Premium offline consumer PE. Right investor for much larger round.', '✅ None', 'Series C+'),
('Barath Shankar Subramanian', 'Accel India', 'Identified', 'P4', 'VC — Tech First', 'accel.com · Barath Shankar LinkedIn', 'accel.com/companies — apply or warm intro', 'Only approach if tech narrative is stronger. Otherwise skip for now.', '2026-04-15', 'No vacation rental conflict. Backed FirstClub. $650M Fund VIII active. BUT: tech-first mandate. Will push on "where is the tech moat?"', '10–25 Cr', 'Good fund but will ask tech moat question hard.', '✅ None', 'Series A'),
('Teruhide Sato', 'BEENEXT', 'Identified', 'P4', 'VC — Singapore/India', 'beenext.com', 'Apply via beenext.com', 'Lower priority — primarily fintech/SaaS focus.', '2026-04-10', 'Singapore-based, very active in India early-stage. $160M fund (India + Japan focus). 261 portfolio cos. BUT: primarily fintech, e-commerce, SaaS.', '1–5 Cr', 'Active India early-stage investor. But no hospitality thesis.', '✅ None', 'Seed / Pre-Series A');
